<!-- Phase 5 website teaching layer; original chapter remains read-only. Evidence: website/reviews/android-phase5-findings.md. -->

<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">A thermometer appears in discovery, connects, then stops sending readings. “Connected” was only one step. A reliable device feature must know which operation is pending, how it ends, and whether the user still wants the session.</p>

<!-- @after BLE Architecture :: animation -->
### Discovery is not readiness

<figure class="stepper" data-no-handoff><span class="stepper-title">One bounded connection attempt</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="node" data-el="radio"><strong>BLE state</strong><small data-text="radioV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="intent"><strong>User intent</strong><small data-text="intentV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="data"><strong>Measurement</strong><small data-text="dataV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{
"label": "Find",
"caption": "With the required permission, scan with a deadline.",
"state": {
"radio": "active"
},
"text": {
"radioV": "scanning",
"intentV": "connect requested",
"dataV": "none"
},
"add": [
"radio",
"intent",
"data"
]
},
{
"label": "Connect",
"caption": "Finding a candidate ends discovery; connection and service discovery still remain.",
"state": {
"radio": "active"
},
"text": {
"radioV": "connecting → discovering"
}
},
{
"label": "Ready",
"caption": "A configured subscription can now deliver data.",
"state": {
"data": "active"
},
"text": {
"radioV": "ready",
"dataV": "reading received"
}
},
{
"label": "Leave",
"caption": "If the user ends the feature, stop owned work rather than reconnecting indefinitely.",
"state": {
"intent": "done",
"radio": "ghost"
},
"text": {
"intentV": "session ended",
"radioV": "stopped"
}
}
]</script><figcaption>Every active state also needs a failure, cancellation and timeout path.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Reliability and Observability :: check -->
### Try the decision

<details><summary>Persist a live GATT object?</summary>

No. A GATT connection belongs to one process and one radio session. Persist the device identity and what the user wanted, then rebuild the connection when the app needs it again.
</details>

<details><summary>Permission granted once: finished?</summary>

No. The user or the system can revoke it later, so check at each use and keep a path for denial or revocation.
</details>

<details><summary>A location is accurate but old. Use it?</summary>

Only if it is fresh enough. Check both the fix's age and its accuracy against what the feature needs; an accurate position from an hour ago can be wrong for this decision.
</details>

<!-- @after Reliability and Observability :: animation -->
### Losing the device and getting it back

<figure class="stepper" data-no-handoff><span class="stepper-title">Reconnect only while the product still needs it</span><div class="stage viz-grid" style="--cols:3"><div class="node" data-el="link"><strong>BLE link</strong><small data-text="linkV">connected</small></div><div class="node" data-el="intent"><strong>Durable intent</strong><small>device ID + "keep syncing"</small></div><div class="node is-key" data-el="retry"><strong>Reconnect policy</strong><small data-text="retryV">idle</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{"label":"Lost","caption":"The peripheral walks out of range and the callback reports a disconnect. The live GATT object is now useless.","add":["link","intent","retry"],"state":{"link":"error"},"text":{"linkV":"disconnected"}},
{"label":"Still wanted?","caption":"Check the durable intent first. If the user has left the feature, stop here; a reconnect loop nobody needs drains the battery.","state":{"intent":"active"}},
{"label":"Bounded retry","caption":"The user still wants syncing, so retry with exponential backoff and jitter, with a limit, as the chapter's Reliability section describes.","state":{"intent":"done","retry":"active"},"text":{"retryV":"backoff with jitter, capped"}},
{"label":"Rebuilt","caption":"The device returns. A new connection is built from the stored device ID, not from the old object, and syncing resumes.","state":{"link":"done","retry":"done"},"text":{"linkV":"new connection","retryV":"reset"}}
]</script><figcaption>Illustrative flow. Use Previous, Next or Play; every step is also readable as text.</figcaption></figure>
